<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Disco starts.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Disco starts.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Smith Barney said on Monday it started coverage of Argentine supermarket chain Disco SA with a rating of neutral, medium risk.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Alejandro Daniel Lerner wrote in a report that he had set a 12-month price target for the stock of $30.</p>
<p>-- He set estimates of earnings per share of $1.40, $1.50 and $1.80 for 1996, 1997 and 1998, respectively.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Disco is solidly positioned with a focused market strategy, strong product mix, a capable management team and an attractive financial position,&quot; Lerner said.</p>
<p>-- The company's shares closed at 26-1/4 on Monday in New York.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
